Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.15,0:00:29.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Shattano, Shattano, Shll,\NChess, Chess, Hazz, Chess,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.69,0:00:40.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.35,0:01:09.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.87,0:01:31.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.99,0:03:02.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, my God.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.71,0:03:51.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you not feeling\Nwell, Mr. Joe Starr? Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.83,0:03:53.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you for asking, Avdol.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.73,0:03:56.89,Default,,0,0,0,,I've had some bad experiences\Nwith planes in the past.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.97,0:03:58.49,Default,,0,0,0,,As I mentioned before,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.75,0:04:02.91,Default,,0,0,0,,we have but 50 days to confront Dio,\Nif we have not succeeded by then.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.01,0:04:07.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, I understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.69,0:04:10.69,Default,,0,0,0,,If we cannot make it in\Ntime, then Holly could die.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.39,0:04:25.22,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.30,0:04:26.13,Default,,0,0,0,,What was that?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.63,0:04:31.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Jostar-san, the engine on the\Nleft side has caught fire.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.95,0:04:33.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Calm down.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.11,0:04:35.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Everyone remain seated.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.73,0:04:38.85,Default,,0,0,0,,But Jostar-san, the engine...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.93,0:04:39.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.27,0:04:42.68,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll go ask the pilots about this myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.45,0:04:50.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Captain, please tell me\Nwhat's happening here.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.99,0:04:52.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm trying to find out.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.39,0:04:54.16,Default,,0,0,0,,We're rapidly losing altitude.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.59,0:04:55.59,Default,,0,0,0,,We're out of control.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.67,0:04:57.55,Default,,0,0,0,,You have to return to your seat.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.75,0:05:00.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Unless we regain control, we're\Ngoing to crash into the ocean.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.41,0:05:02.01,Default,,0,0,0,,What did you say?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.81,0:05:09.99,Default,,0,0,0,,What a pain.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.43,0:05:42.31,Default,,0,0,0,,The important thing is\Nthat everyone is all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.39,0:05:44.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Many ships travel through these waters.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.87,0:05:48.03,Default,,0,0,0,,They'll pick up our distress signal\Nand surely come to our rescue.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.11,0:05:49.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I sure hope you're right about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.99,0:05:52.97,Default,,0,0,0,,We certainly can't afford to hang\Naround in a place like this for long.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.05,0:05:56.51,Default,,0,0,0,,But I wonder, could our enemies\Nhave caused this accident?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.47,0:06:05.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.85,0:06:10.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm, my friends, it seems that\Nour luck has not run out just yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.21,0:06:12.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.13,0:06:20.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Please signal them.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.97,0:06:53.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Right then, now we can go back.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.79,0:06:57.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Guess we shouldn't take my natural\Ngood luck too lightly, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.25,0:07:02.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Is something bothering you, Avdol?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.75,0:07:04.69,Default,,0,0,0,,The ramp has already been lowered for us,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.77,0:07:08.18,Default,,0,0,0,,but why aren't any of the crew\Nmembers showing themselves?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.87,0:07:41.55,Default,,0,0,0,,No one's coming to meet us.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.67,0:07:45.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Just where the hell is the crew, anyway?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.31,0:07:48.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Just like that famous abandoned\Nship, the Mary Celeste.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.49,0:07:51.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.40,0:07:52.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Is there anyone here?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.03,0:07:54.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Anyone here?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.67,0:07:55.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Anyone here?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.03,0:07:59.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Is there anyone here?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.85,0:08:02.03,Default,,0,0,0,,He's here! He's here!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.19,0:08:03.05,Default,,0,0,0,,He's here!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.19,0:08:05.01,Default,,0,0,0,,He's here! He's here!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.53,0:08:08.88,Default,,0,0,0,,In any case, let's investigate the ship.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.21,0:08:25.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Is something wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.67,0:08:29.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Look at this window.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.89,0:08:33.77,Default,,0,0,0,,How could they have spotted us\Nthrough a window as filthy as that?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.69,0:08:44.81,Default,,0,0,0,,It appears there is no one\Nin the engine room either.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.41,0:08:56.03,Default,,0,0,0,,So there's no one on board.\NWhat was that? Just now?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.43,0:09:01.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Josa, what is it? There\Nwas a sound from inside!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.31,0:09:17.05,Default,,0,0,0,,What a gigantic monkey.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.25,0:09:23.21,Default,,0,0,0,,This appears to be an orangutan.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.13,0:09:30.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Is he telling us to open the cage?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.07,0:09:32.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Certainly looks like it to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.29,0:09:44.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, you're a pretty\Nsmart guy for a monkey.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.25,0:09:46.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Please be careful.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.57,0:09:49.31,Default,,0,0,0,,An orangutan is five times\Nstronger than a human,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.39,0:09:51.51,Default,,0,0,0,,so he could easily rip your arm off.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.23,0:09:54.41,Default,,0,0,0,,He's not starving.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.69,0:09:58.93,Default,,0,0,0,,which means there's at least one\Nperson on board who's been feeding him.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.85,0:10:00.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Right, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.01,0:10:02.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go find the owner.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.23,0:10:14.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.47,0:10:20.30,Default,,0,0,0,,What the?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.75,0:10:32.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm, look up there, on the bridge.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.31,0:10:41.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.79,0:10:47.83,Default,,0,0,0,,This is a ghost ship. Ridiculous.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.97,0:11:03.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I think it would be best\Nif we all stay together.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.07,0:11:07.93,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you think?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.01,0:11:08.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Anyone?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.41,0:11:11.00,Default,,0,0,0,,This ship is too dangerous.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.21,0:11:13.92,Default,,0,0,0,,What can we do now in\Nthe middle of the ocean?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.19,0:11:17.01,Default,,0,0,0,,But we're not sure where\Nthe ship is headed yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.41,0:11:22.24,Default,,0,0,0,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.05,0:11:26.76,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess we'll have to go see.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.39,0:11:28.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.13,0:12:00.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Bonjour, Monsieur Joestar.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.05,0:12:02.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Greetings to your party.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.13,0:12:05.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, you! Wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.65,0:12:12.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell me, how is it you know about us?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.87,0:12:19.09,Default,,0,0,0,,A man with a birthmark\Nshaped like this told me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.29,0:12:25.59,Default,,0,0,0,,You're one of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.47,0:12:31.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Justice! Look out!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.57,0:12:34.41,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.35,0:12:46.19,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.93,0:12:51.67,Default,,0,0,0,,My Stan's name is Silver Chariot.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.97,0:12:55.61,Default,,0,0,0,,So, Avdol, it would appear that\Nyou are very anxious to die.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.19,0:13:01.09,Default,,0,0,0,,I made a clock out of fire on that table.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.47,0:13:04.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Before it burns 12 o\N'clock, I will kill you.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.17,0:13:07.23,Default,,0,0,0,,That was very formidable swordplay.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.39,0:13:08.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I am truly in awe.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.25,0:13:11.65,Default,,0,0,0,,But you say you would\Nkill me by 12 o 'clock.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.73,0:13:12.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Well,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.64,0:13:16.95,Default,,0,0,0,,don't you think that you are being just\Na little bit too vain, man from France?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.39,0:13:19.05,Default,,0,0,0,,My greeting is overdue.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.33,0:13:21.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Please allow me to introduce myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.51,0:13:25.97,Default,,0,0,0,,My name is Polnareff,\NJean-Pierre Polnareff.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.51,0:13:28.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Merci beaucoup.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.49,0:13:30.77,Default,,0,0,0,,My sincere thanks for your introduction.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.85,0:13:31.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Now that...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.15,0:13:35.61,Default,,0,0,0,,All Avdol's stand did was move its arm,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.69,0:13:38.35,Default,,0,0,0,,and the lower half of the\Ntable has burned away.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.43,0:13:40.97,Default,,0,0,0,,It is very important that you realize my
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.05,0:13:43.75,Default,,0,0,0,,stand's fire is not like\Nsome ordinary flame.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.99,0:13:48.55,Default,,0,0,0,,And because my stand can control fire\Nat will, it is called Magician's Red.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.69,0:13:50.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm. Impressive.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.35,0:13:54.53,Default,,0,0,0,,But a while ago, you said I was too vain.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.15,0:13:57.87,Default,,0,0,0,,You think I'm vain about\Nmy swordplay skill?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.09,0:14:04.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Too vain, you said?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.99,0:14:06.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you still say that now?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.91,0:14:09.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Amazing.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.82,0:14:12.90,Default,,0,0,0,,He was able to pierce five\Ncoins with a single thrust.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.07,0:14:14.87,Default,,0,0,0,,No, there's more to it than that.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.95,0:14:16.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Take another look at those coins.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.31,0:14:20.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I see what you mean.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.71,0:14:24.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Very good, so you understand\Nwhat this means then.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.89,0:14:28.51,Default,,0,0,0,,My stand can cut, parry and block\Nyour fire with complete control.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.59,0:14:33.12,Default,,0,0,0,,In other words, my friend, this means\Nyou are virtually powerless against me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.53,0:14:36.75,Default,,0,0,0,,When did he...?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.87,0:14:43.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Avdol, I could kill you here and now,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.33,0:14:45.71,Default,,0,0,0,,but the size of this room\Nput you at a disadvantage.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.79,0:14:50.07,Default,,0,0,0,,A more open space would allow you to\Nuse your ability at full power, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.15,0:14:53.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Beating you there would be a more\Nsuitable victory for my stand.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.45,0:14:54.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Everyone, get in line.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.07,0:14:57.48,Default,,0,0,0,,One by one, I will cut each of you apart.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.43,0:15:09.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, Avdol, Mr.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.01,0:15:12.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Joestar, please do not\Ninterfere with this.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.77,0:15:17.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Just as he said, with this much open\Nspace, I can more freely use my stand.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.99,0:15:20.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I will predict your destiny.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.95,0:15:25.19,Default,,0,0,0,,I predict that you will destroy\Nyourself with your own stance abilities.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.99,0:15:36.09,Default,,0,0,0,,What happened to your vaunted flame?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.17,0:15:39.29,Default,,0,0,0,,If you're not going to\Nbreathe fire, then I'll start.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.51,0:15:53.51,Default,,0,0,0,,That man certainly got a\Nlot of bloody nerve while he
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.59,0:15:56.65,Default,,0,0,0,,was just waiting for\NMagician's Red to breathe fire.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.57,0:16:00.73,Default,,0,0,0,,You don't stand a chance against me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.61,0:16:05.83,Default,,0,0,0,,He's coming for real this time.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.25,0:16:13.78,Default,,0,0,0,,By Jove, I wouldn't want to get\Nbroiled by this next attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.27,0:16:16.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Crossfire coming here!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.59,0:16:18.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.45,0:16:21.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Is that really all the power you've got?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.17,0:16:24.65,Default,,0,0,0,,If so...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.69,0:16:28.83,Default,,0,0,0,,The stand's flame was too powerful.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.13,0:16:30.72,Default,,0,0,0,,It's burning Avdol instead.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.37,0:16:34.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Just as I said, right, Monsieur Avdol?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.27,0:16:38.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, what a desperate struggle, eh?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.07,0:16:41.61,Default,,0,0,0,,What is this resistance?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.01,0:16:46.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Once again, now, let's fire!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.41,0:16:52.85,Default,,0,0,0,,His stand is melting.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.71,0:16:54.99,Default,,0,0,0,,He's badly burned.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.25,0:16:57.49,Default,,0,0,0,,He's lucky he's only severely injured.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.69,0:17:00.45,Default,,0,0,0,,No, perhaps I should say he's unlucky.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.73,0:17:03.71,Default,,0,0,0,,In any case, he won't be able\Nto get up for three months.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.79,0:17:07.11,Default,,0,0,0,,His stand has been reduced to\Na pulp and is unable to fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.19,0:17:08.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, Mr.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.10,0:17:12.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Joestar, we should start talking about\Nthe best way to get to Egypt from here.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.07,0:17:17.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Look up there!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.53,0:17:19.36,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.47,0:17:24.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't believe it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.97,0:17:26.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Bravo!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.17,0:17:28.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Bravo!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.01,0:17:33.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Why is his body floating there in midair?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.87,0:17:36.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Look carefully through\Nthe eyes of your stands.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.65,0:17:40.01,Default,,0,0,0,,His stand.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.45,0:17:47.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Allow me to present Silver Chariot\Nwithout his protective armor.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.87,0:17:51.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, you look appropriately amazed.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.71,0:17:56.01,Default,,0,0,0,,If you don't mind, please explain\Nto me how this is possible. Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.35,0:17:58.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Your attitude is most commendable.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.63,0:18:01.83,Default,,0,0,0,,The explosion earlier was not\Nmy stand being blown to bits,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.91,0:18:04.85,Default,,0,0,0,,but the impact of my stand\Nthrowing off his armor.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.37,0:18:09.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Only his armor was burned by your fire,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.77,0:18:12.65,Default,,0,0,0,,so I was able to get by\Nwith only minor injuries.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.45,0:18:16.93,Default,,0,0,0,,And now, with the armor\Ngone, I can move much faster.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.23,0:18:19.49,Default,,0,0,0,,So you're saying that\Nthe weight of your armor
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.57,0:18:22.57,Default,,0,0,0,,prevented you from avoiding\Nmy crossfire hurricane?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.65,0:18:25.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Oui, that is correct.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.87,0:18:28.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Which means that without\Nyour protective armor,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.39,0:18:31.39,Default,,0,0,0,,you would not survive being\Nstruck by another CFH.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.31,0:18:35.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Oui, but that is impossible. Impossible?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.23,0:18:37.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.14,0:18:40.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Because I'm about to show you\Nsomething that will horrify you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.25,0:18:45.31,Default,,0,0,0,,What the it can't be a person. Should only
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.39,0:18:49.79,Default,,0,0,0,,have one stand hmm you\Nappear to be horrified?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.87,0:18:53.89,Default,,0,0,0,,These after images affect not just your\Nsight but your other senses as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.97,0:18:56.17,Default,,0,0,0,,How about this sword play now!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.67,0:19:06.93,Default,,0,0,0,,That was an after image your stunts\Nare useless against my stand now!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.27,0:19:12.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Avdol!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.65,0:19:19.71,Default,,0,0,0,,You should know that I developed a\Nvariation on my crossfire hurricane attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.91,0:19:22.59,Default,,0,0,0,,The unkshake fire is\Nnormally a single flame,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.79,0:19:26.20,Default,,0,0,0,,but I can break it up and hurl\Nit as many separate flames.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.31,0:19:35.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Now really, Avdol!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.49,0:19:37.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Not good.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.63,0:19:39.59,Default,,0,0,0,,His stands have formed a defensive circle.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.67,0:19:42.44,Default,,0,0,0,,He'll strike the flames\Nback, just like before.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.95,0:19:44.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Easy, easy, easy, easy!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.09,0:19:50.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I will strike them back.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.89,0:19:56.01,Default,,0,0,0,,What the...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.19,0:20:08.07,Default,,0,0,0,,That is the hole Polnareff's stand made\Nearlier when he struck back Avdol's flames.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.61,0:20:12.89,Default,,0,0,0,,I get it now.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.19,0:20:16.53,Default,,0,0,0,,He made use of a hole created\Nin the midst of battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.77,0:20:18.93,Default,,0,0,0,,His ability to split the\Nflame made it possible
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.01,0:20:21.42,Default,,0,0,0,,for him to pull off this clever strategy.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.31,0:20:32.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Burning to death would be\Na very painful way to die.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.65,0:20:35.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Use that blade and put\Nan end to your misery.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.69,0:20:58.81,Default,,0,0,0,,I was so vain, thinking my swordplay\Nwould never be beaten by mere flames.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.17,0:21:02.94,Default,,0,0,0,,For that, I choose to\Nburn to death gracefully.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.07,0:21:05.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Consider this to be a\Nsalute to your abilities
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.41,0:21:07.76,Default,,0,0,0,,from the one who you defeated in battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.95,0:21:14.59,Default,,0,0,0,,His proud spirit goes beyond Dio's orders.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.87,0:21:19.45,Default,,0,0,0,,This man who remains true to the code\Nof honor that you call chivalry. Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.75,0:21:22.81,Default,,0,0,0,,If we let him die like this,\Nwe may regret it later.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:23.11,0:21:27.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Perhaps there's a very good reason why\Nthis man became one of Dio's assassins.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.31,0:21:32.41,Default,,0,0,0,,We're safe now.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.61,0:21:34.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Our enemy has been defeated.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.95,0:21:38.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I have to admit, you really\Nhad me worried for a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.23,0:21:39.06,Default,,0,0,0,,What a relief.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.35,0:21:46.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, watch out!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.95,0:21:59.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Hit the deck!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:25.63,0:22:27.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Damn, Ape is a stand user.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:32.31,0:22:35.43,Default,,0,0,0,,He turned that bolt into a pipe. Jotaro!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:38.73,0:22:39.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Chariot!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:39.71,0:22:41.59,Default,,0,0,0,,This entire ship is his...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:41.67,0:22:43.03,Default,,0,0,0,,His stand!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:54.79,0:22:56.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, monkey.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:56.49,0:22:58.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Your hairy ass is next.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:07.81,0:23:09.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Jotaro!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:24.61,0:23:25.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Jotaro!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:55.51,0:23:57.53,Default,,0,0,0,,It seems to be over now.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:01.35,0:24:06.67,Default,,0,0,0,,But whether this boat will break down\Nor reach land, Is anyone's guess.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:07.11,0:24:11.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Who would have imagined his stand\Nmade use of a little boat like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:11.35,0:24:16.00,Default,,0,0,0,,If we'd known this would happen, maybe\Nwe would have tried to tame that monkey.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:18.81,0:24:22.29,Default,,0,0,0,,He's really something to have recovered\Nfrom those injuries so quickly.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:22.37,0:24:26.59,Default,,0,0,0,,There must be something important he\Nfeels he must accomplish in this life.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:26.67,0:24:31.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Otherwise, no matter how young he is, he\Nwould not have been able to heal this fast.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:34.19,0:24:35.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Mr.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:35.10,0:24:40.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Joestar, I may be prying, but I have\Nnoticed that you're always wearing gloves.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:40.35,0:24:43.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Please don't tell me that your\Nleft hand is actually a right hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:43.89,0:24:45.42,Default,,0,0,0,,My left hand a right hand?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:45.53,0:24:47.97,Default,,0,0,0,,That is a very peculiar question to ask.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:48.17,0:24:52.88,Default,,0,0,0,,For a long time, I've been searching for\Na man whose hands are both right hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:58.23,0:25:02.11,Default,,0,0,0,,This is an honorable wound I\Nreceived in battle 50 years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:02.47,0:25:03.47,Default,,0,0,0,,My apologies.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:03.91,0:25:04.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Please forgive me.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:05.89,0:25:08.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Polnareff, would you kindly\Ntell us what this is all about?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:08.99,0:25:13.11,Default,,0,0,0,,I've been looking for the man who\Nbrutally murdered my younger sister.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:14.71,0:25:17.21,Default,,0,0,0,,It happened three years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:22.51,0:25:26.99,Default,,0,0,0,,That day my sister was walking\Nhome from school with a classmate
Dialogue: 0,0:26:15.91,0:26:20.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know his face, but his\Nhands are both right hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:21.35,0:26:24.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Obviously, someone\Npossessing a stand ability.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:26.23,0:26:28.81,Default,,0,0,0,,I made a vow that he would pay for all the
Dialogue: 0,0:26:28.89,0:26:31.77,Default,,0,0,0,,things he did to my younger\Nsister with his life.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:35.77,0:26:39.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Then, one year ago, I met Dio.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:44.09,0:26:45.95,Default,,0,0,0,,But, who are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:47.07,0:26:51.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I can see a man, boldly\Nconfronting you in your mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:52.63,0:26:55.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Listen, how about you\Nand I become friends?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:56.27,0:27:00.51,Default,,0,0,0,,If you will help me with my\Nwork, I will lend you a hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:01.27,0:27:03.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Perhaps I can find that man for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:05.13,0:27:07.83,Default,,0,0,0,,So, I was ordered to kill you all,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:07.97,0:27:11.21,Default,,0,0,0,,and even though I knew it\Nwas a whisper from the devil,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:11.79,0:27:15.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd made a deal to get the information\NI needed to avenge my sisters.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:16.43,0:27:17.26,Default,,0,0,0,,death.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:17.34,0:27:20.80,Default,,0,0,0,,He's very good at finding and taking\Nadvantage of people's weaknesses.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:20.89,0:27:22.97,Default,,0,0,0,,And according to the\Nstory he just told us,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:23.05,0:27:26.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Dio already knew the identity of\Nthe man who killed his sister.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:26.83,0:27:27.66,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:28.69,0:27:31.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Polnareff, what are you going to do now?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:31.73,0:27:34.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd like to join you guys\Non your mission to find Dio.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:35.05,0:27:38.87,Default,,0,0,0,,If I go after him too, I might\Nmeet the man who killed my sister.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:39.35,0:27:40.79,Default,,0,0,0,,A jolly good idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:41.07,0:27:44.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Our goals may be different, but\Nour destination is the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:45.71,0:27:46.75,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:46.95,0:27:49.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's stop messing around\Nand get our butts to Egypt.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:49.67,0:27:51.23,Default,,0,0,0,,This is going to be a blast.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:51.31,0:27:56.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, those Egyptian women are so mysterious\Nand appealing that I can hardly wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:56.63,0:28:00.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought he was a man who lived\Nby a code of honor and chivalry,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:00.23,0:28:01.64,Default,,0,0,0,,but now I'm not so sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:02.03,0:28:04.27,Default,,0,0,0,,His mood certainly changes in a hurry.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:04.81,0:28:08.40,Default,,0,0,0,,His mind and his instincts seem\Nto be completely independent.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:10.63,0:28:11.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, what a pain.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:23.77,0:28:24.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Strength.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:24.68,0:28:25.97,Default,,0,0,0,,So useless.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:26.77,0:28:31.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Not only that, even the chariot\NPolnareff double-crossed us.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:33.29,0:28:37.53,Default,,0,0,0,,However, all the cards of\Ndestiny still remain in my hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:40.97,0:28:43.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't allow this to trouble you, Lord Dio.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:43.95,0:28:47.79,Default,,0,0,0,,No matter how many of those\Nuseless worms defect to the enemy,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:48.07,0:28:50.48,Default,,0,0,0,,they can never be a match for your power.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:50.65,0:28:55.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Besides that, the Emperor and the Hanged\NMan are already on their way to India.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:56.29,0:28:57.85,Default,,0,0,0,,One of them will do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:58.19,0:29:01.78,Default,,0,0,0,,The Hanged Man's right hand\Nwill take care of them for sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:04.03,0:29:07.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Because the Master of\Nthe Invincible Stand,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:07.35,0:29:11.03,Default,,0,0,0,,the Hanged Man, he is\Nmy precious dearest son.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:11.11,0:29:13.57,Default,,0,0,0,,His name is J. Gaia!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:41.11,0:29:41.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:42.81,0:30:44.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go.
